  body: "# Bereavement Benefit between earlier and BSP regimes\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter introduces
    Bereavement Benefit from 9 April 2001 and distinguishes BSP for deaths from 6 April 2017, while earlier Widow’s
    Benefits may continue subject to their conditions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe BB family includes distinct
    payment and allowance routes; it is not interchangeable with BSP. Surviving cohabiting partners and the 2023
    remedial order are explicitly present later in the chapter and must not be excluded using introductory wording
    alone.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 63001, PDF page 1](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=1).\n\
    - [DMG 63002, PDF page 1](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=1).\n\
    - [DMG 63007, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=4).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=8).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=9).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 32](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=32).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 33](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=33).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch63`:
    PDF `7f894b8bac8a4056f9b89fff0df4cdb4231c1c2b187de78b5c64b6cc33636d88`; extracted pages `ed410bfb75f7f3ac15120a0dd10024bfb246faea02695229229deaed09d9033e`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.914779Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=1
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/wpa-remedial-transition
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter includes specific 2023 protection for existing WPA and entitlement of certain
      cohabiting partners.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch63/0028
      quote: "63088 Claimants that have been in receipt of WPA before 9.2.23 do not lose their entitlement for the\n\
        \n duration of their award as a result of the Remedial Order 1.\n\n\n                                  \
        \                 1 Bereavement Benefits (Remedial) Order 2023 art 2(1)"
      locator: DMG 63088
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch63/0028
      quote: "63089 A claimant may have been entitled to WPA before the Remedial Order came into force as a result\n\
        of the death of their spouse or civil partner because they had not divorced. From 9.2.23, the deceased’s\n\
        co-habiting partner may also become entitled for the same period and the Remedial Order enables both\nclaimants
        to receive WPA"
      locator: DMG 63089
